{
  "algorithm": "iff-x402-requirement-fingerprint-v1",
  "description": "Cross-language test vectors for the IFF x402 requirement fingerprint (spec doc: docs/TRANSPARENCY_LOG_PLAN.md, contract C1). option_fp = hex(sha256(\"iff-x402-option/v1\\n\" + canonical_json(option))); set_fp = hex(sha256(\"iff-x402-set/v1\\n\" + join(sort(unique(option_fp...)), \"\\n\"))). canonical_json has exactly the keys scheme, network, asset, pay_to, amount in that order, compact (no inserted whitespace), and must not HTML-escape '\u003c', '\u003e', '\u0026'. Normalization: scheme/network = TrimSpace then lowercase. asset/pay_to = lowercase only when the trimmed value matches ^0x[0-9a-fA-F]{40}$; otherwise TrimSpace only (base58 and other non-hex addresses stay case-sensitive). amount = TrimSpace, then strip leading zeros only when the trimmed value is purely ASCII decimal digits (\"000\" -\u003e \"0\"); otherwise the trimmed value is used as-is. max_timeout_seconds is never part of the hashed shape. Phase 2 (contract C4 rule 4b) adds payee_fingerprints/payee_set_fingerprint to every vector below: payee_fp = hex(sha256(\"iff-x402-payee/v1\\n\" + canonical_json({scheme,network,asset,pay_to}))) -- the same canonical_json and normalization rules as option_fp, but with the amount key omitted entirely and a different domain-separation prefix; payee_set_fp = hex(sha256(\"iff-x402-set/v1\\n\" + join(sort(unique(payee_fp...)), \"\\n\"))), reusing the exact same set-level domain prefix and aggregation as set_fp (safe because the option-level domain prefixes already differ, so a payee_fp can never collide with an option_fp for the same bytes). Two option sets that differ only in amount therefore always share a payee_set_fingerprint even though their set_fingerprint differs -- see payee_fingerprint_shared_across_amount_a/b.",
